1
00:00:00,174 --> 00:00:05,264
China's biggest weak spot is a strip
of water only 2.7 kilometres wide.

2
00:00:05,374 --> 00:00:07,064
India sits right at its mouth.

3
00:00:07,145 --> 00:00:10,555
The Strait of Malacca links the
Indian Ocean to the Pacific.

4
00:00:10,655 --> 00:00:12,265
At its narrowest, near Singapore,

5
00:00:12,655 --> 00:00:15,465
it is only about 2.7 kilometres wide.

6
00:00:15,606 --> 00:00:17,656
Roughly a quarter of the
world's traded goods,

7
00:00:17,946 --> 00:00:21,481
and a large share of China's oil imports,
sail through it.

8
00:00:21,481 --> 00:00:23,491
Planners call it China's Malacca dilemma:

9
00:00:23,901 --> 00:00:26,971
one chokepoint,
with the Indian Ocean on one side.

10
00:00:27,002 --> 00:00:30,432
India's Andaman and Nicobar Islands
sit at the western entrance,

11
00:00:30,822 --> 00:00:34,452
only about 150 kilometres
from Indonesia's coast.

12
00:00:34,632 --> 00:00:35,522
Reality check:

13
00:00:35,892 --> 00:00:38,962
blocking a busy international
strait would be an act of war,

14
00:00:39,172 --> 00:00:42,792
and ships could reroute through longer
channels like the Sunda and Lombok

15
00:00:42,792 --> 00:00:43,562
straits.

16
00:00:43,582 --> 00:00:47,442
China is also building pipelines
and ports, in Myanmar and Pakistan,

17
00:00:47,442 --> 00:00:49,123
to cut the risk.

18
00:00:49,123 --> 00:00:51,013
Is a chokepoint a weakness or a strength?

19
00:00:51,208 --> 00:00:51,838
Comment.

